[CENTER][SIZE=7][COLOR=#9B59B6][B]AntiEnchants[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][COLOR=#95A5A6][I]Ban, cap and control enchantments — server-wide.[/I][/COLOR][/SIZE]

[COLOR=#E74C3C][B]Ban[/B][/COLOR]  ·  [COLOR=#F1C40F][B]Cap[/B][/COLOR]  ·  [COLOR=#2ECC71][B]Exempt[/B][/COLOR]  ·  [COLOR=#3498DB][B]Compensate[/B][/COLOR]  ·  [COLOR=#9B59B6][B]Bypass[/B][/COLOR][/CENTER]

Born as [I]AntiMending[/I], now a general-purpose enchantment control plugin: decide which enchantments exist on your server, at which level, on which items, in which worlds — and who is allowed to skip the rules.

[SIZE=5][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Features[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][COLOR=#E74C3C][B]Ban any enchantment[/B][/COLOR] (default: mending). Removed from player inventories, pickups, fishing, chest loot and mob drops — it can't exist on your server.
[*][COLOR=#F1C40F][B]Level caps[/B][/COLOR] — don't ban it, cap it. [ICODE]sharpness: 3[/ICODE] reduces every Sharpness IV/V to III automatically.
[*][COLOR=#2ECC71][B]Item whitelist[/B][/COLOR] — exempt item types from all checks, with wildcards: [ICODE]exempt-items: [ "*_SWORD", "BOW" ][/ICODE]
[*][COLOR=#3498DB][B]Compensation[/B][/COLOR] (optional) — when an enchantment is stripped, the player gets something back (XP bottles, emeralds, anything), per enchantment or globally.
[*][COLOR=#9B59B6][B]Permission bypasses[/B][/COLOR] — [ICODE]antienchants.bypass.mending[/ICODE] for donor ranks, staff or quest winners. [ICODE]antienchants.bypass.*[/ICODE] for everything. Nodes default to FALSE, so ops never bypass by accident.
[*][COLOR=#1ABC9C][B]Per-world rules[/B][/COLOR] — ban fortune only in your resource world, cap efficiency only in the mining world. Plus [ICODE]disabled-worlds[/ICODE] to turn the plugin off entirely somewhere.
[*][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Blocks at the source[/B][/COLOR] — enchanting table results and anvil/grindstone previews are cleaned [B]before[/B] the player pays.
[*][COLOR=#C0392B][B]Blocks mending's effect[/B][/COLOR] — XP never repairs durability, even if an item slips through.
[*][COLOR=#8E44AD][B]Curses[/B][/COLOR] — [ICODE]ban-all-curses: true[/ICODE] blocks every curse at once (vanilla + other plugins).
[*][COLOR=#27AE60][B]Villager control[/B][/COLOR] — stop librarians from selling enchanted books (or any book), and any trade carrying a banned/over-cap enchantment.
[*][COLOR=#2980B9][B]Player feedback[/B][/COLOR] — configurable MiniMessage messages when items are stripped, capped or compensated. Empty = silent.
[*][COLOR=#7F8C8D][B]Audit log[/B][/COLOR] (optional) — every strip goes to [ICODE]strips.log[/ICODE]: when, who, where, what.
[*][COLOR=#16A085][B]Other plugins' enchantments[/B][/COLOR] — keys accept any namespace ([ICODE]ecoenchants:telekinesis[/ICODE]).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Commands[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]  [COLOR=#95A5A6](permission [ICODE]antienchants.admin[/ICODE], alias /ae)[/COLOR]
[LIST]
[*][ICODE]/ae reload[/ICODE] — [COLOR=#95A5A6]reload the config, no restart.[/COLOR]
[*][ICODE]/ae list[/ICODE] — [COLOR=#95A5A6]what's banned and capped right now.[/COLOR]
[*][ICODE]/ae check[/ICODE] — [COLOR=#95A5A6]inspect the item in your hand.[/COLOR]
[*][ICODE]/ae add <enchant>[/ICODE] / [ICODE]/ae remove <enchant>[/ICODE] — [COLOR=#95A5A6]edit the banlist live (saved to config).[/COLOR]
[*][ICODE]/ae cap <enchant> <level|off>[/ICODE] — [COLOR=#95A5A6]set or clear a level cap live.[/COLOR]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Config (excerpt)[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[CODE=yaml]
banned-enchantments:
  keys:
    - mending
  ban-all-curses: false
  exempt-items: []          # e.g. [ "*_SWORD", "BOW" ]

level-caps: {}              # e.g. sharpness: 3

compensation:
  enabled: false
  default:
    - "EXPERIENCE_BOTTLE:4"
  per-enchant: {}           # e.g. mending: [ "EMERALD:8" ]

per-world: {}               # extra bans/caps per world
[/CODE]
Everything is config-gated. Updating the jar adds new options to your config automatically — your edited values are never touched, and old configs keep working without regeneration.

[SIZE=5][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Servers using AntiEnchants[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[CENTER][IMG]https://bstats.org/signatures/bukkit/AntiEnchants.svg[/IMG][/CENTER]
[COLOR=#95A5A6]Anonymous stats via bStats — opt-out in [ICODE]plugins/bStats/config.yml[/ICODE].[/COLOR]

[SIZE=5][COLOR=#E67E22][B]Requirements[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]
Paper (or fork) [B]1.21+[/B]. No dependencies.

Suggestions and bug reports are welcome in the discussion thread.
